{# Default alert actions for EVERY saved search below.

   Splunk `.conf` files have NO prefix-based stanza inheritance -- a stanza
   named `[Foo - bar]` inherits nothing from `[Foo]` (verified empirically
   against Splunk 10.2.0: a child stanza read back the global default
   severity and an empty cron). `[default]` is the only inheritance
   mechanism savedsearches.conf offers, and it is scoped to the app that
   declares it -- also measured: a `[default]` in a throwaway app reached
   its own searches and none of the 787 owned by the other 24 apps.

   So delivery is declared ONCE here instead of per-stanza. Adding a saved
   search below gets Slack with no per-search configuration; there is no
   macro to remember to call. Replaces alert_deliver(), deleted with
   savedsearches/00-macros.j2.

   $name$ is the stanza name, so the message needs no per-search title.
   The action stays gated on its credential being present: enabling an
   action whose alert_actions.conf half is unconfigured fires the alert and
   then fails delivery silently.

   Slack rides the [slack] action shipped by the official "Slack
   Notification Alert" app (Splunkbase 2878, splunk/slack-alerts --
   splunk_docker_addons in vars/addons.yml). A prior [webhook]-based
   attempt failed Slack's incoming-webhook payload validation with 400 --
   Splunk's built-in webhook action sends a fixed JSON schema it cannot
   customize, and Slack requires {"text": ...}. This app's alert action
   generates that shape itself; alert_actions.conf.j2 sets its global
   default webhook URL, `message` is the one required per-search param.

   Zammad is declared below but NOT a working channel -- no Zammad alert
   action is installed anywhere (Vikunja 2150), and
   assert_alerting_gates.yml fails the converge if its gate variable is
   ever set for exactly that reason. The block stays as the landing point
   for when that work ships, not as evidence delivery works today.
#}
[default]
{% if splunk_docker_alert_slack_webhook %}
action.slack = 1
action.slack.param.message = [$name$] $job.resultCount$ result(s) — $view_link$
{% endif %}
{% if splunk_docker_alert_zammad_token %}
action.zammad = 1
action.zammad.param.group = {{ splunk_docker_alert_zammad_group }}
action.zammad.param.priority = 2 normal
action.zammad.param.state = new
action.zammad.param.correlation_key = $name$
{% endif %}

